WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.835 --> 00:00:03.912
The plan to move line 3 to hall B is ready.

2
00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:07.975
Now the sponsor, the team and you have to get to work together.

3
00:00:08.994 --> 00:00:12.233
Between the plan and the run lie meetings and sessions.

4
00:00:13.287 --> 00:00:15.806
Four topics, from the meeting to the shop floor.

5
00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.159
The first topic is Which meeting when.

6
00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:24.984
Each meeting format has a purpose, participants, a duration and an output.

7
00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.995
A meeting shares or decides.

8
00:00:28.732 --> 00:00:30.613
A workshop makes something together.

9
00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:34.974
Before the work begins, you hold a kick-off with the team.

10
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.923
There you fix the goal, the roles and the first steps.

11
00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:43.292
Two days ahead you send round a one-page pre-read.

12
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:46.626
That way the kick-off is about agreements.

13
00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:50.937
The second topic is Designing and leading a workshop.

14
00:00:52.004 --> 00:00:53.699
A workshop has one purpose.

15
00:00:54.402 --> 00:00:57.339
It delivers a visible output you can photograph.

16
00:00:58.379 --> 00:00:59.703
You are the facilitator.

17
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.235
You lead the process and do not steer the content.

18
00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:08.932
The group draws the process of line 3 with sticky notes on a brown paper.

19
00:01:09.959 --> 00:01:13.651
First how it really goes, not how the procedure says it should.

20
00:01:15.026 --> 00:01:18.184
The third topic is Ideas and decisions in a group.

21
00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:20.874
How do we get the switchboard in time?

22
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.143
First many ideas, then choose.

23
00:01:24.865 --> 00:01:28.964
We do that on an online whiteboard, a shared board with sticky notes.

24
00:01:29.972 --> 00:01:33.083
Everyone starts with silent writing, without judging.

25
00:01:33.809 --> 00:01:35.887
That way quiet people count too.

26
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.638
Similar ideas go together.

27
00:01:39.388 --> 00:01:40.828
That is affinity grouping.

28
00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.586
The group chooses with dots.

29
00:01:44.332 --> 00:01:46.375
The top three get an owner and a date.

30
00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:50.113
The fourth topic is Formats on the floor.

31
00:01:50.856 --> 00:01:53.503
Reports and meetings show what people say.

32
00:01:54.174 --> 00:01:56.124
The shop floor shows what happens.

33
00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:57.927
There are four.

34
00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:02.831
The gemba walk, the interview round, the demo and the kaizen event.

35
00:02:03.895 --> 00:02:05.694
You hold an interview round.

36
00:02:06.476 --> 00:02:09.529
One-to-one conversations with people from every level.

37
00:02:10.536 --> 00:02:15.308
Every conversation follows the same interview guide, with five open questions.

38
00:02:16.619 --> 00:02:18.279
This is the map of Projects.

39
00:02:18.993 --> 00:02:22.232
Formats and meetings lies between Plan and Run.

40
00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.016
Formats and meetings has four topics, each with four levels.

41
00:02:28.039 --> 00:02:30.825
Start with Which meeting when, at Basics level.

42
00:02:31.866 --> 00:02:35.233
At Working knowledge you hold a kick-off, draw a process,

43
00:02:35.419 --> 00:02:38.623
run an online idea session and an interview round.

44
00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.720
At Advanced you design the meeting system and the session,

45
00:02:42.847 --> 00:02:45.482
choose who decides and which format fits.

46
00:02:46.502 --> 00:02:49.497
At Expert you weigh meeting load and legitimacy,

47
00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.015
facilitate as a craft and commission a kaizen event.

48
00:02:54.089 --> 00:02:57.339
After that comes Run, where the project keeps moving.
